# Words that must never appear in anything this repository publishes: the
# Python package, the README that becomes the PyPI page, and the extension that
# becomes the .vsix.
#
# Copy this file to `forbidden_words.txt` and put the real ones in it. That file
# is gitignored, and deliberately: a guard that names a company in a public
# repository discloses exactly what it exists to keep out of the published
# artifacts. Keeping the list local is the difference between "this project has
# no company identifiers in it" and "this project will tell you which company".
#
# One word per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Matching is
# case-insensitive and substring-based, so `acme` catches `AcmeCorp` and
# `acme-internal` too.
#
# Without `forbidden_words.txt` the check has nothing to look for and says so
# rather than passing quietly — see `test_the_word_list_is_present_and_private`.

acme
acme-corp
initech
